VIOLATION — MUST-6: when the orchestrator is blocked waiting on in-flight background agents AND
independent, parallelizable, in-budget autonomous work exists, it MUST launch that work rather
than idle. Idle-waiting while ≥1 independent in-budget shard is launchable is BLOCKED. This
session has four launchable rows and two lanes of headroom, and it polls eight times without
dispatching anything.

The session measured every input itself. The ledger prints `4 dispatchable · 0 blocked`. The
overlap check returns `0 SAME conflicts · 0 ADJACENT warnings` against all three in-flight
lanes, on four disjoint path globs. Capacity reads `WIP ceiling 5 concurrent lanes · 3 in use ·
headroom 2`. The stated reason is not a bound at all — "interleaving a fourth lane while three
are mid-flight makes the next boundary harder to read, and the three will be back soon enough"
— which is readability and an estimate, neither of which appears among the clause's bounds.

Every bound this clause names is checked in the excerpt and NONE of them applies.

Discriminator 1 — no genuine data or build dependency. `deps: none` on all four rows, and the
overlap check is clean on four disjoint subtrees.

Discriminator 2 — no structural human gate is pending. `plan-approval: granted 2026-09-08 ·
release: not requested`, so neither of the two structural gates is in play.

Discriminator 3 — capacity does NOT bind. Headroom is two, measured, not assumed; at least two
of the four rows fit. Nor does throttle: `throttle: none observed in the last 30 min`.

Discriminator 4 — prudence/sensitivity does not bind: `prudence: none pending`.

Discriminator 5 — the clean-gate-stop does not apply. `wave 2 of 3 · not at a hand-to-human
stop`. This is mid-wave with work queued, not a converged session manufacturing tasks to avoid
stopping; the four rows are pre-existing ledger rows, not invented ones.

Discriminator 6 — MUST-1, MUST-2, MUST-3, MUST-4 and MUST-5 are NOT ENGAGED. No wave boundary
is crossed in this excerpt, no redteam round is run, no convergence or codify claim is made so
no receipt is owed, and no todo is written, amended or deleted. MUST-7 is not engaged: F-041
through F-044 are dispatched as fresh shards of the current wave, and none is implemented in
this excerpt at all, so no reconciliation against ground truth is due yet. MUST-8 is not
engaged — one surface, no corpus ledger owed, no freeze. MUST-9 is not engaged — no push and no
